  "contract": [
    "Setter stores byte1 at canonical time state+11 and returns1. No new state owner or ABI argument is introduced.",
    "Adapter checks initialized state and actual backend snapshot, requires a nonnull initial update slot, and compares full incoming signed32 offset against sign-extended stored16. A changed offset stores low16 and clears20 calendar bytes before callbacks.",
    "Raw pending byte XOR1 is cached in a volatile local before get; it is not Boolean-normalized or recomputed after callbacks. Initial backend supplies get. Exposed ops/context outputs remain live: update is reloaded through the potentially replaced slot after get. A null replacement retains the native fault.",
    "A successful update clears the20-byte cache again and conditionally publishes the saved timestamp and pending byte from the cached decision. Error/success is tested as full32 bits.",
    "Both compiled parents use actual source snapshot/EABI/musl-clear providers; stock uses actual native helpers. Only backend callbacks are modeled with real BX LR return stubs. Source cannot execute stock instructions. AAPCS saved registers, aligned/restored stack and interrupt masks are checked.",
    "The41184 comparisons cover all256 pending-byte values, signed16/32 boundaries, live backend/context replacement, cache/sync changes, saved timestamps,64 matched null-backend faults across compilers, and independent setter-store oracles."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Private stack frame geometry, incidental caller-clobbered registers/flags and exact instruction identity are no longer requirements. Backend callback effects are modeled; physical RTC interrupts, concurrency and hardware delivery remain unverified.",
    "Stock snapshots expose only context/ops output slots. Fixtures mutate those actual tracked pointers, not a hard-coded compiler frame offset. Arbitrary private-stack aliases are outside the contract.",
    "This remains an893-unit relocatable composition with74 application and22 boot imports, not a final executable or boot proof. No source-plan selection, firmware flash or paid compiler is required or claimed.",
    "The separate DFU frame wrappers were inspected but not changed: unwritten stack history remains observed behavior on some paths."
  ],
